day movie probably our favorite  movie and in fact when we got married  once we were husband and wife and they  said i pronounce you husband wife you  can kiss the bride and we walked off as  mr and miss lachey  to the song that they did in the movie  the beatles song so  that's how much we loved the movie it  has all the things there you go  any changes to love is blind season two  honestly the biggest change is for me  and nick so for season one when you were  watching love is blind you only saw us i  think it was like six moments but we  were there the entire  was eight weeks we prepped we were with  them every day we saw them before they  went in the pods after the pots we  weren't there at night time when they  went in pods but we were there for a lot  of the narrowing down we were there for  proposals we were hiding in the back  rooms before they went in after they  came out we were there for all of it  obviously when they edited it and got it  together for season two they're like  really we just used you guys for the  intro when they get to their destination  and then we were there for all the  weddings we got to see all the weddings  i got to talk to lauren before she  walked down the aisle with cameron i got  to talk to amber before she walked down  the aisle with barnett and nick talked  to barnett and nick talked to cameron  which is why when we shot the reunion i  literally was brought to tears in some  of the questions because i felt like i  really truly knew these people's love  story season two i was looking at a  paper with their name and their photo  and so i didn't get to really know their  story  as much and that for that i'm bummed out  about but i do know that they brought it  that's just my humble opinion on drew  love i'm vanessa lachey and i co-host  love is blind on netflix with my husband  nick lachey and keep an eye out for  season two  and three  [Music]  you
 

